---
description: Rules for rapid prototype work
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is for high-fidelity product prototypes and usability tests.

- Prioritise testable user flows over production architecture.
- Use existing shadcn components before creating new primitives.
- Build responsive, accessible interfaces with keyboard support and visible focus states.
- Keep prototype state local or in localStorage unless explicitly asked otherwise.
- Put mock content in src/data; do not invent a backend.
- Include realistic empty, loading, success, and error states where relevant.
- Avoid adding dependencies without explaining why.
- Do not refactor unrelated code while implementing a test.
- Before considering a flow complete, verify the primary task can be completed end-to-end.